 "ideas": {
  "momentum": "At each month end hold the 5 stocks that rose most over the 11 months ending a month ago. Why: winners of the past year have tended to keep winning for some months.",
  "low_vol": "At each month end hold the 5 stocks whose price moved least from day to day over the last 60 days. Why: steady stocks have tended to return more than their risk suggests.",
  "high52": "Buy on the first close above every close of the past 250 days (after 20 days without one). Sell after 20 trading days, or earlier on a close 8% below the entry. Why: a new one-year high is news that holders anchored to the old high are slow to price.",
  "pullback": "In a stock above its 200-day average, buy after 3 lower closes in a row that add up to a fall of 5% or more. Sell on the first close above the 5-day average, or after 10 trading days. Why: sharp dips inside an uptrend have tended to be bought back.",
  "losers": "At each week end hold the 5 stocks that fell most over the last 5 trading days, for one week. Why: the past week's biggest losers have tended to bounce the week after.",
  "volume_surge": "Buy at the close of a day the stock rose 4% or more on at least 3 times its usual volume. Sell after 10 trading days, or earlier on a close 8% below the entry. Why: big news is absorbed over days, not in one."
 },
